<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n71488" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξεν-ᾰπάτης</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[πᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξειν-</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπατάω</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who cheats strangers,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>O.</u>
				10(11).34
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>one who betrays his host,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ibyc.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				1790i10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Med.</u>
				1392
			</span></i> (anap.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>a treacherous breeze</i> within a harbour, while another is
			blowing at sea, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AB</u>
				109
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
